# 32. Groups `()`

Parentheses are used to create groups.

Example:

```python
import re

text = "My date is 02-09-2026"

pattern = r"(\d{2})-(\d{2})-(\d{4})"

result = re.search(pattern, text)

print(result.group())
print(result.group(1))
print(result.group(2))
print(result.group(3))
```

Output:

```text
02-09-2026
02
09
2026
```

