# 33. Named Groups

We can give names to groups.

Example:

```python
import re

text = "Name: Niranjan, Age: 21"

pattern = r"Name: (?P<name>\w+), Age: (?P<age>\d+)"

result = re.search(pattern, text)

print(result.group("name"))
print(result.group("age"))
```

Output:

```text
Niranjan
21
```

This makes complex regex easier to understand.

