# 47. Real-World Cybersecurity Example — Log Analysis

Imagine a server log:

```text
192.168.1.10 - LOGIN SUCCESS
192.168.1.20 - LOGIN FAILED
10.0.0.5 - LOGIN FAILED
192.168.1.10 - LOGIN SUCCESS
```

We want to find failed login attempts.

```python
import re

log = """
192.168.1.10 - LOGIN SUCCESS
192.168.1.20 - LOGIN FAILED
10.0.0.5 - LOGIN FAILED
192.168.1.10 - LOGIN SUCCESS
"""

failed = re.findall(r"(\d{1,3}(?:\.\d{1,3}){3}).*LOGIN FAILED", log)

print(failed)
```

Output:

```text
['192.168.1.20', '10.0.0.5']
```

This demonstrates how regex can help a SOC analyst extract suspicious IP addresses from logs.

