# 56. Regex Pipeline

Regex becomes especially powerful when combined with other Python features.

Example:

```python
import re

log = """
2026-09-01 192.168.1.10 LOGIN FAILED
2026-09-01 10.0.0.5 LOGIN SUCCESS
2026-09-01 192.168.1.20 LOGIN FAILED
"""

ips = re.findall(
    r"\b(?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}\b",
    log
)

for ip in ips:
    print(ip)
```

Output:

```text
192.168.1.10
10.0.0.5
192.168.1.20
```

Regex can therefore become part of an automated cybersecurity pipeline:

```text
Log File
   ↓
Python
   ↓
Regex
   ↓
Extract Data
   ↓
Analyze Data
   ↓
Generate Alert
```

