# 58. Common Mistakes

## Mistake 1 — Forgetting `r`

Instead of:

```python
"\d+"
```

prefer:

```python
r"\d+"
```

---

## Mistake 2 — Using `match()` when you need `search()`

Remember:

```text
match()  → beginning
search() → anywhere
```

---

## Mistake 3 — Forgetting `+`

This:

```regex
\d
```

matches one digit.

This:

```regex
\d+
```

matches one or more digits.

For:

```text
12345
```

`\d` finds individual digits, while `\d+` finds the whole number.

---

## Mistake 4 — Regex is not always the best solution

Don't use complicated regex when a simple string operation is enough.

Good programming means choosing the simplest tool that solves the problem.

