# 62. Cybersecurity Practice Project

## 🔐 Mini Project: Failed Login Detector

Create a Python program that reads a log and identifies failed login attempts.

Example log:

```text
192.168.1.10 LOGIN SUCCESS
192.168.1.20 LOGIN FAILED
192.168.1.30 LOGIN FAILED
10.0.0.5 LOGIN SUCCESS
```

Expected output:

```text
Failed login detected from: 192.168.1.20
Failed login detected from: 192.168.1.30
```

Possible solution:

```python
import re

log = """
192.168.1.10 LOGIN SUCCESS
192.168.1.20 LOGIN FAILED
192.168.1.30 LOGIN FAILED
10.0.0.5 LOGIN SUCCESS
"""

pattern = r"\b(?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}\b.*LOGIN FAILED"

matches = re.findall(pattern, log)

for match in matches:
    ip = re.search(r"\b(?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}\b", match)
    print("Failed login detected from:", ip.group())
```

This is a simple example of how Python + Regex can be used for **security log analysis**.

